      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-285212",
      ":question/problem": "In a science experiment, Priya heated a metal rod and then left it to cool in a room that maintained a constant temperature of $65^{\u2218}F$. At $3:00$ p.m., the rod\u2019s temperature was $200^{\u2218}F$. After $5$ minutes, its temperature had dropped to $170^{\u2218}F$, and after $10$ minutes, it was $146.5^{\u2218}F$. The rod continued to cool over time.\n\nWhich of the following functions best models the temperature $T(t)$ in degrees Fahrenheit of the rod $t$ minutes after it was removed from the heat?"
